<Base lang="en" alt="confidentialitate/" title="Privacy" description="What data we keep when you ask a question on the radar, why, and how to delete it.">
  <h1>Privacy</h1>
  <p>The analyses can be read without an account and without leaving any data. We keep the data below only if you ask a question.</p>
  <h2>Who is responsible for the data</h2>
  <p>EtiQ Events SRL, VAT number RO 30586107. Contact: <a href="mailto:nitadanielcristian@gmail.com">nitadanielcristian@gmail.com</a>.</p>
  <h2>What we keep and why</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><b>Your email address</b>: so you can have an account (we verify the address with an email) and so we can send you the answer. We never see the password: Firebase handles it. We do not publish it, sell it or send marketing messages to it.</li>
    <li><b>The display name, the question and the page</b> you asked on: so we can answer you.</li>
    <li><b>Consent to publish</b>: the question and the answer appear publicly, with the display name, only if you ticked the consent box.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>The legal basis is your consent, which you give when you send the question.</p>
  <h2>Where it is kept</h2>
  <p>In the Firebase service (Google), with the database in a European Union region. We prepare the answers with the help of an AI assistant and check them before publishing.</p>
  <h2>How long, and how to delete it</h2>
  <p>We keep the questions as long as the account exists. You can delete a question at any time from <a href={`${import.meta.env.BASE_URL}en/account/`}>your account</a>. To delete the account or exercise any other right (access, rectification, objection), write to the address above. You can lodge a complaint with the Romanian data protection authority (ANSPDCP).</p>
</Base>
